msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operations and observables"
msgstr "Operasi dan boleh cerap Pauli"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore tensoring */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore tensoring */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli matrices play a central role in the stabilizer formalism.\n"
"We'll begin the lesson with a discussion of Pauli matrices, including some of their basic algebraic properties, and we'll also discuss how Pauli matrices (and tensor products of Pauli matrices) can describe measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Pauli memainkan peranan utama dalam formalisme penstabil.\n"
"Kita akan mulakan pelajaran ini dengan perbincangan mengenai matriks Pauli, termasuk beberapa sifat algebra asasnya, dan kita juga akan membincangkan bagaimana matriks Pauli (dan hasil darab tensor matriks Pauli) boleh menggambarkan pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operation basics {#pauli-operation-basics}"
msgstr "Asas operasi Pauli {#pauli-operation-basics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are the Pauli matrices, including the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and "
"the three non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah matriks Pauli, termasuk matriks identiti $2\\times 2$ dan tiga"
" matriks Pauli bukan-identiti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"X =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & -i\\\\\n"
"  i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"X =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & -i\\\\\n"
"  i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Properties of Pauli matrices {#properties-of-pauli-matrices}"
msgstr "Sifat matriks Pauli {#properties-of-pauli-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All four of the Pauli matrices are both unitary and Hermitian.\n"
"We used the names $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ and $\\sigma_z$ to refer to the non-identity Pauli matrices earlier in the series, but it is conventional to instead use the capital letters $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z$ in the context of error correction.\n"
"This convention was followed in the previous lesson, and we'll continue to do this for the remaining lessons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesemua empat matriks Pauli adalah unitari dan Hermitian.\n"
"Kita menggunakan nama $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ dan $\\sigma_z$ untuk merujuk kepada matriks Pauli bukan-identiti di awal siri ini, tetapi adalah lazim untuk menggunakan huruf besar $X,$ $Y,$ dan $Z$ dalam konteks pembetulan ralat.\n"
"Konvensyen ini diikuti dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, dan kita akan terus berbuat demikian untuk pelajaran-pelajaran yang tinggal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Different non-identity Pauli matrices *anti-commute* with one another.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Pauli bukan-identiti yang berbeza *anti-tukar ganti* antara satu "
"sama lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"XY = -YX \\qquad XZ = -ZX \\qquad YZ = -ZY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"XY = -YX \\qquad XZ = -ZX \\qquad YZ = -ZY\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These anti-commutation relations are simple and easy to verify by performing the multiplications, but they're critically important, in the stabilizer formalism and elsewhere.\n"
"As we will see, the minus signs that emerge when the ordering between two different non-identity Pauli matrices is reversed in a matrix product correspond precisely to the detection of errors in the stabilizer formalism.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hubungan anti-tukar ganti ini mudah dan boleh disahkan dengan melakukan pendaraban, tetapi ia sangat penting, dalam formalisme penstabil dan di tempat lain.\n"
"Seperti yang akan kita lihat, tanda negatif yang muncul apabila susunan antara dua matriks Pauli bukan-identiti yang berbeza dibalikkan dalam hasil darab matriks sepadan tepat dengan pengesanan ralat dalam formalisme penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We also have the multiplication rules listed here.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga mempunyai peraturan pendaraban yang disenaraikan di sini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"XX = YY = ZZ = \\mathbb{I} \\qquad\n"
"XY = iZ \\qquad YZ = iX \\qquad ZX = iY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"XX = YY = ZZ = \\mathbb{I} \\qquad\n"
"XY = iZ \\qquad YZ = iX \\qquad ZX = iY\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, each Pauli matrix is its own inverse (which is always true for any matrix that is both unitary and Hermitian), and multiplying two different non-identity Pauli matrices together is always $\\pm i$ times the remaining non-identity Pauli matrix.\n"
"In particular, up to a phase factor, $Y$ is equivalent to $X Z,$ which explains our focus on $X$ and $Z$ errors and apparent lack of interest in $Y$ errors in quantum error correction;\n"
"$X$ represents a bit-flip, $Z$ represents a phase-flip, and so (up to a global phase factor) $Y$ represents both of those errors occurring simultaneously on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, setiap matriks Pauli adalah inversnya sendiri (yang sentiasa benar untuk mana-mana matriks yang unitari dan Hermitian), dan mendarab dua matriks Pauli bukan-identiti yang berbeza sentiasa menghasilkan $\\pm i$ kali matriks Pauli bukan-identiti yang tinggal.\n"
"Khususnya, sehingga faktor fasa, $Y$ bersamaan dengan $X Z,$ yang menjelaskan tumpuan kita pada ralat $X$ dan $Z$ serta kekurangan minat yang nyata (seolah-olah) terhadap ralat $Y$ dalam pembetulan ralat kuantum;\n"
"$X$ mewakili balik-bit, $Z$ mewakili balik-fasa, dan jadi (sehingga faktor fasa global) $Y$ mewakili kedua-dua ralat itu berlaku serentak pada qubit yang sama.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli operations on multiple qubits {#pauli-operations-on-multiple-qubits}"
msgstr ""
"Operasi Pauli pada berbilang qubit {#pauli-operations-on-multiple-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four Pauli matrices all represent operations (which could be errors) on a single qubit — and by tensoring them together we obtain operations on multiple qubits.\n"
"As a point of terminology, when we refer to an *n-qubit Pauli operation*, we mean a tensor product of any $n$ Pauli matrices, such as the examples shown here, for which $n=9.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Keempat-empat matriks Pauli mewakili operasi (yang boleh menjadi ralat) pada satu qubit — dan dengan mendarab tensorkannya (hasil darab tensor antaranya), kita memperoleh operasi pada berbilang qubit.\n"
"Sebagai istilah, apabila kita merujuk kepada *operasi Pauli n-qubit*, kita bermaksud hasil darab tensor mana-mana $n$ matriks Pauli, seperti contoh-contoh yang ditunjukkan di sini, di mana $n=9.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Often, the term *Pauli operation* refers to a tensor product of Pauli matrices *along with a phase factor,* or sometimes just certain phase factors such as $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm i.$\n"
"There are good reasons to allow for phase factors like this from a mathematical viewpoint — but, to keep things as simple as possible, we'll use the term *Pauli operation* in this course to refer to a tensor product of Pauli matrices without the possibility of a phase factor different than 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selalunya, istilah *operasi Pauli* merujuk kepada hasil darab tensor matriks Pauli *bersama-sama faktor fasa,* atau kadangkala hanya faktor fasa tertentu seperti $\\pm 1$ dan $\\pm i.$\n"
"Terdapat sebab-sebab yang baik untuk membenarkan faktor fasa seperti ini dari sudut pandang matematik — tetapi, untuk memastikan perkara mudah, kita akan menggunakan istilah *operasi Pauli* dalam kursus ini untuk merujuk kepada hasil darab tensor matriks Pauli tanpa kemungkinan faktor fasa selain 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *weight* of an $n$-qubit Pauli operation is the number of non-identity Pauli matrices in the tensor product.\n"
"For instance, the first example above has weight $0,$ the second has weight $2,$ and the third has weight $6.$\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the weight of an $n$-qubit Pauli operation is the number of qubits on which it acts non-trivially.\n"
"It's typical that quantum error correcting codes are designed so that they can detect and correct errors represented by Pauli operations so long as their weight isn't too high.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Berat* suatu operasi Pauli $n$-qubit ialah bilangan matriks Pauli bukan-identiti dalam hasil darab tensor.\n"
"Contohnya, contoh pertama di atas mempunyai berat $0,$ yang kedua mempunyai berat $2,$ dan yang ketiga mempunyai berat $6.$\n"
"Secara intuitif, berat suatu operasi Pauli $n$-qubit ialah bilangan qubit yang ia bertindak secara bukan-trivial.\n"
"Adalah tipikal bahawa kod pembetulan ralat kuantum direka supaya boleh mengesan dan membetulkan ralat yang diwakili oleh operasi Pauli selagi beratnya tidak terlalu tinggi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operations as generators {#pauli-operations-as-generators}"
msgstr "Operasi Pauli sebagai penjana {#pauli-operations-as-generators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's sometimes useful to consider collections of Pauli operations as *generators* of sets (more specifically, *groups*) of operations, in an algebraic sense that you may recognize if you're familiar with group theory.\n"
"If you're not familiar with group theory, that's OK — it's not essential for the lesson.\n"
"A familiarity with the basics of group theory is, however, strongly recommended for those interested in exploring quantum error correction in greater depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kadangkala berguna untuk menganggap koleksi operasi Pauli sebagai *penjana* set (lebih khusus, *kumpulan*) operasi, dalam erti algebra yang mungkin anda kenali jika anda biasa dengan teori kumpulan.\n"
"Jika anda tidak biasa dengan teori kumpulan, tidak mengapa — ia tidak penting untuk pelajaran ini.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, kebiasaan dengan asas-asas teori kumpulan amat disyorkan bagi mereka yang berminat untuk meneroka pembetulan ralat kuantum dengan lebih mendalam.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $P_1, \\ldots,  P_r$ are $n$-qubit Pauli operations.\n"
"When we refer to the *set generated* by $P_1, \\ldots, P_r,$ we mean the set of *all* matrices that can be obtained by multiplying these matrices together, in any combination and in any order we choose, taking each one as many times as we like.\n"
"The notation used to refer to this set is $\\langle P_1, \\ldots, P_r \\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan bahawa $P_1, \\ldots,  P_r$ ialah operasi Pauli $n$-qubit.\n"
"Apabila kita merujuk kepada *set yang dijana* oleh $P_1, \\ldots, P_r,$ kita bermaksud set *semua* matriks yang boleh diperoleh dengan mendarab matriks-matriks ini bersama, dalam sebarang gabungan dan dalam sebarang urutan yang kita pilih, mengambil setiap satu sebanyak mana kali yang kita suka.\n"
"Notasi yang digunakan untuk merujuk set ini ialah $\\langle P_1, \\ldots, P_r \\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, the set generated by the three non-identity Pauli matrices is "
"as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, set yang dijana oleh tiga matriks Pauli bukan-identiti "
"adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Y, Z \\rangle = \\bigl\\{\\alpha P\\,:\\,\\alpha\\in\\{1,i,-1,-i\\},\\; P\\in\\{\\mathbb{I},X,Y,Z\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Y, Z \\rangle = \\bigl\\{\\alpha P\\,:\\,\\alpha\\in\\{1,i,-1,-i\\},\\; P\\in\\{\\mathbb{I},X,Y,Z\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through the multiplication rules listed earlier.\n"
"There are 16 different matrices in this set, which is commonly called the *Pauli group*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini boleh difahami melalui peraturan pendaraban yang disenaraikan sebelumnya.\n"
"Terdapat 16 matriks berbeza dalam set ini, yang biasanya dipanggil *kumpulan Pauli*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a second example, if we remove $Y,$ we obtain half of the Pauli group.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh kedua, jika kita mengeluarkan $Y,$ kita memperoleh separuh "
"daripada kumpulan Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}, X, Z, -iY, -\\mathbb{I}, -X, -Z, iY \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}, X, Z, -iY, -\\mathbb{I}, -X, -Z, iY \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's one final example (for now), where this time we have $n=2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah satu contoh terakhir (buat masa ini), di mana kali ini kita "
"mempunyai $n=2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X \\otimes X, Z \\otimes Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, X\\otimes X, Z\\otimes Z, -Y\\otimes Y \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X \\otimes X, Z \\otimes Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, X\\otimes X, Z\\otimes Z, -Y\\otimes Y \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case we obtain just four elements, owing to the fact that $X\\otimes"
" X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ commute:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes ini kita hanya memperoleh empat elemen, disebabkan oleh hakikat "
"bahawa $X\\otimes X$ dan $Z\\otimes Z$ bertukar ganti:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(X\\otimes X)(Z\\otimes Z) & = (XZ) \\otimes (XZ)\\\\\n"
"& = (-ZX)\\otimes (-ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (ZX)\\otimes (ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (Z\\otimes Z)(X\\otimes X).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(X\\otimes X)(Z\\otimes Z) & = (XZ) \\otimes (XZ)\\\\\n"
"& = (-ZX)\\otimes (-ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (ZX)\\otimes (ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (Z\\otimes Z)(X\\otimes X).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli observables {#pauli-observables}"
msgstr "Boleh cerap Pauli {#pauli-observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli matrices, and $n$-qubit Pauli operations more generally, are unitary, and therefore they describe unitary operations on qubits.\n"
"But they're also *Hermitian* matrices, and for this reason they describe *measurements,* as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Pauli, dan operasi Pauli $n$-qubit secara amnya, adalah unitari, dan oleh itu ia menggambarkan operasi unitari pada qubit.\n"
"Tetapi ia juga adalah matriks *Hermitian*, dan atas sebab ini ia menggambarkan *pengukuran,* seperti yang akan dijelaskan sekarang.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hermitian matrix observables {#hermitian-matrix-observables}"
msgstr "Boleh cerap matriks Hermitian {#hermitian-matrix-observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first an arbitrary Hermitian matrix $A.$\n"
"When we refer to $A$ as an *observable*, we're associating with $A$ a certain uniquely defined projective measurement.\n"
"In words, the possible outcomes are the distinct eigenvalues of $A,$ and the projections that define the measurement are the ones that project onto the spaces spanned by the corresponding eigenvectors of $A.$\n"
"So, the outcomes for such a measurement happen to be real numbers — but because matrices have only finitely many eigenvalues, there will only be finitely many different measurement outcomes for a given choice of $A.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan dahulu matriks Hermitian sewenang-wenangnya $A.$\n"
"Apabila kita merujuk $A$ sebagai *boleh cerap*, kita mengaitkan dengan $A$ suatu pengukuran projektif yang ditakrifkan secara unik.\n"
"Dalam kata lain, hasil yang mungkin ialah nilai eigen yang berbeza bagi $A,$ dan unjuran yang mentakrifkan pengukuran ialah yang mengunjurkan ke ruang yang direntangi oleh vektor eigen yang sepadan bagi $A.$\n"
"Jadi, hasil untuk pengukuran sedemikian kebetulannya adalah nombor nyata — tetapi kerana matriks hanya mempunyai bilangan nilai eigen yang terhingga, hanya akan ada bilangan hasil pengukuran yang terhingga untuk sesuatu pilihan $A.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In greater detail, by the spectral theorem, it is possible to write\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih terperinci, mengikut teorem spektrum, adalah mungkin untuk "
"menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\lambda_k \\Pi_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\lambda_k \\Pi_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for *distinct* real number eigenvalues $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ and "
"projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m$ satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk nilai eigen nombor nyata *berbeza* $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ dan"
" unjuran $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m$ yang memenuhi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1 + \\cdots + \\Pi_m = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1 + \\cdots + \\Pi_m = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Such an expression of a matrix is unique up to the ordering of the eigenvalues.\n"
"Another way to say this is that, if we insist that the eigenvalues are ordered in decreasing value $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_2 > \\cdots > \\lambda_m,$ then there's only one way to write $A$ in the form above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ungkapan matriks sedemikian adalah unik sehingga pengurutan nilai eigen.\n"
"Cara lain untuk menyatakannya ialah, jika kita menegaskan bahawa nilai eigen disusun dalam nilai menurun $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_2 > \\cdots > \\lambda_m,$ maka hanya ada satu cara untuk menulis $A$ dalam bentuk di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on this expression, the measurement we associate with the observable "
"$A$ is the projective measurement described by the projections "
"$\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m,$ and the eigenvalues $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$"
" are understood to be the measurement outcomes corresponding to these "
"projections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan ungkapan ini, pengukuran yang kita kaitkan dengan boleh cerap "
"$A$ ialah pengukuran projektif yang diterangkan oleh unjuran "
"$\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m,$ dan nilai eigen $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ "
"difahami sebagai hasil pengukuran yang sepadan dengan unjuran-unjuran ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurements from Pauli operations {#measurements-from-pauli-operations}"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran daripada operasi Pauli {#measurements-from-pauli-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's see what measurements of the sort just described look like for Pauli operations, starting with the three non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
"These matrices have spectral decompositions as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lihat bagaimana rupa pengukuran seperti yang baru diterangkan untuk operasi Pauli, bermula dengan tiga matriks Pauli bukan-identiti.\n"
"Matriks-matriks ini mempunyai penguraian spektrum seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"X = \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert - \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Y = \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert - \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Z = \\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert - \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"X = \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert - \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Y = \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert - \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Z = \\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert - \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurements defined by $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z,$ viewed as observables, are therefore the projective measurements defined by the following\n"
"sets of projections, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran yang ditakrifkan oleh $X,$ $Y,$ dan $Z,$ dilihat sebagai boleh "
"cerap, adalah oleh itu pengukuran projektif yang ditakrifkan oleh set "
"unjuran berikut, masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert, \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert \\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert, \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert, \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert \\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert, \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In all three cases, the two possible measurement outcomes are the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1.$\n"
"Such measurements are commonly called $X$-measurements, $Y$-measurements, and $Z$-measurements.\n"
"We encountered these measurements in the \"General measurements\" lesson of \"General formulation of quantum information,\"\n"
"where they arose in the context of quantum state tomography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ketiga-tiga kes, dua hasil pengukuran yang mungkin ialah nilai eigen $+1$ dan $-1.$\n"
"Pengukuran sedemikian biasanya dipanggil pengukuran-$X$, pengukuran-$Y$, dan pengukuran-$Z$.\n"
"Kita telah temui pengukuran-pengukuran ini dalam pelajaran \"Pengukuran am\" bagi \"Rumusan am maklumat kuantum,\"\n"
"di mana ia timbul dalam konteks tomografi keadaan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, a $Z$-measurement is essentially just a standard basis "
"measurement and an $X$ measurement is a measurement with respect to the "
"plus/minus basis of a qubit — but, as these measurements are described here,"
" we're taking the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1$ to be the actual measurement "
"outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tentunya, pengukuran-$Z$ pada asasnya hanyalah pengukuran asas piawai dan "
"pengukuran-$X$ ialah pengukuran terhadap asas plus/minus suatu qubit — "
"tetapi, seperti yang diterangkan di sini, kita mengambil nilai eigen $+1$ "
"dan $-1$ sebagai hasil pengukuran yang sebenar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same prescription can be followed for Pauli operations on $n\\geq 2$ qubits, though it must be stressed that there will still be just two possible outcomes for the measurements described in this way: $+1$ and $-1,$ which are the only possible eigenvalues of Pauli operations.\n"
"The two corresponding projections will therefore have rank higher than one in this case.\n"
"More precisely, for every non-identity $n$-qubit Pauli operation, the $2^n$ dimensional state space always splits into two subspaces of eigenvectors having equal dimension, so the two projections that define the associated measurement will both have rank $2^{n-1}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaedah yang sama boleh diikuti untuk operasi Pauli pada $n\\geq 2$ qubit, walaupun harus ditekankan bahawa masih hanya akan ada dua hasil yang mungkin untuk pengukuran yang diterangkan dengan cara ini: $+1$ dan $-1,$ yang merupakan satu-satunya nilai eigen yang mungkin bagi operasi Pauli.\n"
"Dua unjuran yang sepadan oleh itu akan mempunyai pangkat lebih tinggi daripada satu dalam kes ini.\n"
"Lebih tepat lagi, untuk setiap operasi Pauli $n$-qubit bukan-identiti, ruang keadaan berdimensi $2^n$ sentiasa terbahagi kepada dua subruang vektor eigen berdimensi sama, jadi dua unjuran yang mentakrifkan pengukuran berkaitan akan kedua-duanya mempunyai pangkat $2^{n-1}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurement described by an $n$-qubit Pauli operation, considered as an observable, is therefore not the same thing as a measurement with respect to an *orthonormal basis* of eigenvectors of that operation, nor is it the same thing as independently measuring each of the corresponding Pauli matrices independently, as observables, on $n$ qubits.\n"
"Both of those alternatives would necessitate $2^n$ possible measurement outcomes, but here we have just the two possible outcomes $+1$ and $-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran yang diterangkan oleh suatu operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, dianggap sebagai boleh cerap, oleh itu bukan perkara yang sama dengan pengukuran terhadap *asas ortonormal* vektor eigen operasi itu, mahupun ia sama dengan mengukur setiap matriks Pauli yang sepadan secara bebas, sebagai boleh cerap, pada $n$ qubit.\n"
"Kedua-dua alternatif itu akan memerlukan $2^n$ hasil pengukuran yang mungkin, tetapi di sini kita hanya mempunyai dua hasil yang mungkin $+1$ dan $-1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, consider the 2-qubit Pauli operation $Z\\otimes Z$ as an observable.\n"
"We can effectively take the tensor product of the spectral decompositions to obtain one for the tensor product.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan operasi Pauli 2-qubit $Z\\otimes Z$ sebagai boleh cerap.\n"
"Kita boleh mengambil hasil darab tensor penguraian spektrum secara berkesan untuk memperoleh satu untuk hasil darab tensor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z\\otimes Z & = (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert) \\otimes (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\bigl( \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert \\bigr) - \\bigl( \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z\\otimes Z & = (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert) \\otimes (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\bigl( \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert \\bigr) - \\bigl( \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That is, we have $Z\\otimes Z = \\Pi_0 - \\Pi_1$ for\n"
msgstr "Iaitu, kita mempunyai $Z\\otimes Z = \\Pi_0 - \\Pi_1$ untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so these are the two projections that define the measurement.\n"
"If, for instance, we were to measure a $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ Bell state nondestructively using this measurement, then we would be certain to obtain the outcome $+1,$ and the state would be unchanged as a result of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, the state would not collapse to $\\vert 00\\rangle$ or $\\vert 11\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"jadi ini ialah dua unjuran yang mentakrifkan pengukuran.\n"
"Jika, misalnya, kita mengukur keadaan Bell $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ secara tidak merosakkan menggunakan pengukuran ini, maka kita pasti akan memperoleh hasil $+1,$ dan keadaan tidak akan berubah akibat pengukuran.\n"
"Khususnya, keadaan tidak akan runtuh kepada $\\vert 00\\rangle$ atau $\\vert 11\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Nondestructive implementation through phase estimation {#nondestructive-"
"implementation-through-phase-estimation}"
msgstr ""
"Pelaksanaan tidak merosakkan melalui anggaran fasa {#nondestructive-"
"implementation-through-phase-estimation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For any $n$-qubit Pauli operation, we can perform the measurement associated"
" with that observable nondestructively using phase estimation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk sebarang operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, kita boleh melakukan pengukuran yang"
" dikaitkan dengan boleh cerap itu secara tidak merosakkan menggunakan "
"anggaran fasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a circuit based on phase estimation that works for any Pauli matrix $P,$ where the measurement is being performed on the top qubit.\n"
"The outcomes $0$ and $1$ of the standard basis measurement in the circuit correspond to the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1,$ just like we usually have for phase estimation with one control qubit.\n"
"(Note that the control qubit is on the bottom in this diagram, whereas in the \"Phase estimation and factoring\"\n"
"lesson of \"Fundamentals of quantum algorithms\" the control qubits were drawn on the top.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah litar berdasarkan anggaran fasa yang berfungsi untuk sebarang matriks Pauli $P,$ di mana pengukuran sedang dilakukan pada qubit atas.\n"
"Hasil $0$ dan $1$ pengukuran asas piawai dalam litar sepadan dengan nilai eigen $+1$ dan $-1,$ seperti yang biasanya kita ada untuk anggaran fasa dengan satu qubit kawalan.\n"
"(Perhatikan bahawa qubit kawalan berada di bawah dalam rajah ini, manakala dalam pelajaran \"Anggaran fasa dan pemfaktoran\"\n"
"bagi \"Asas algoritma kuantum\" qubit kawalan dilukis di atas.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-Pauli.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit for measuring a Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-Pauli.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A similar method works for Pauli operations on multiple qubits.\n"
"For example, the following circuit diagram illustrates a nondestructive measurement of the $3$-qubit Pauli observable $P_2\\otimes P_1\\otimes P_0,$ for any choice of $P_0,P_1,P_2 \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaedah yang serupa berfungsi untuk operasi Pauli pada berbilang qubit.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, rajah litar berikut menggambarkan pengukuran tidak merosakkan boleh cerap Pauli $3$-qubit $P_2\\otimes P_1\\otimes P_0,$ untuk sebarang pilihan $P_0,P_1,P_2 \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a 3-qubit Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-3-qubit-Pauli.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit for measuring a 3-qubit Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-3-qubit-Pauli.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This approach generalizes to $n$-qubit Pauli observables, for any $n,$ in the natural way.\n"
"Of course, we only need to include controlled-unitary gates for *non-identity* tensor factors of Pauli observables when implementing such measurements; controlled-identity gates are simply identity gates and can therefore be omitted.\n"
"This means that lower weight Pauli observables require smaller circuits to be implemented through this approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan ini digeneralisasikan kepada boleh cerap Pauli $n$-qubit, untuk sebarang $n,$ dengan cara semula jadi.\n"
"Tentunya, kita hanya perlu menyertakan get unitari-terkawal untuk faktor tensor *bukan-identiti* bagi boleh cerap Pauli apabila melaksanakan pengukuran sedemikian; get identiti-terkawal hanyalah get identiti dan oleh itu boleh ditinggalkan.\n"
"Ini bermakna boleh cerap Pauli berberat rendah (berat yang lebih rendah) memerlukan litar yang lebih kecil untuk dilaksanakan melalui pendekatan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, irrespective of $n,$ these phase-estimation circuits have just a single control qubit, which is consistent with the fact that there are just two possible measurement outcomes for these measurements.\n"
"Using more control qubits wouldn't reveal additional information because these measurements are already perfect using a single control qubit.\n"
"(One way to see this is directly from the general procedure for phase estimation: the assumption $U^2 = \\mathbb{I}$ renders any additional control qubits beyond the first pointless.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa, tanpa mengira $n,$ litar anggaran fasa ini hanya mempunyai satu qubit kawalan, yang konsisten dengan fakta bahawa hanya ada dua hasil pengukuran yang mungkin untuk pengukuran-pengukuran ini.\n"
"Menggunakan lebih banyak qubit kawalan tidak akan mendedahkan maklumat tambahan kerana pengukuran ini sudah sempurna menggunakan satu qubit kawalan.\n"
"(Satu cara untuk melihat ini ialah secara langsung dari prosedur umum anggaran fasa: andaian $U^2 = \\mathbb{I}$ menjadikan sebarang qubit kawalan tambahan selepas yang pertama tidak berguna.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a specific example, of a nondestructive implementation of a "
"$Z\\otimes Z$ measurement, which is relevant to the description of the 3-bit"
" repetition code as a stabilizer code that we'll see shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah contoh khusus, pelaksanaan tidak merosakkan pengukuran "
"$Z\\otimes Z,$ yang berkaitan dengan penerangan kod pengulangan 3-bit "
"sebagai kod penstabil yang akan kita lihat tidak lama lagi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a ZZ observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-ZZ.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit for measuring a ZZ observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-ZZ.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, and for tensor products of more than two $Z$ observables more "
"generally, the circuit can be simplified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes ini, dan untuk hasil darab tensor lebih daripada dua boleh cerap "
"$Z$ secara amnya, litar boleh dipermudahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simplified circuit for measuring a ZZ "
"observable](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/simplified-ZZ.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Simplified circuit for measuring a ZZ "
"observable](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/simplified-ZZ.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, this measurement is equivalent to nondestructively measuring the "
"parity (or XOR) of the standard basis states of two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu, pengukuran ini bersamaan dengan mengukur pariti (atau XOR) keadaan"
" asas piawai dua qubit secara tidak merosakkan.\n"
